                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]The Good[/h1]\n+Sweet sci-fi story, told from a fun POV (you're a sentient robot vacuum)\n+Excellent voice acting — Sabrina's performance is genuinely emotional\n+Minimalist, gorgeous smart-home setting\n+Nice touches: book quotes, appliance \"relationships\"\n+Short, but leaves you wanting more instead of overstaying its welcome\n\n[h1]The Bad[/h1]\n-Gameplay is just point/click/collect — no real challenge\n-Puzzles are too easy for a story about piecing together a mystery\n-Dialogue choices are cosmetic; story doesn't actually branch\n\n[h1]The Buggy[/h1]\n3 achievements currently broken\n\nStory: Rumu, an AI vacuum, tries to uncover what happened to the family that owned him. Along the way it explores consciousness, belonging, and family through smart, well-acted dialogue. Short but satisfying — even got me adding sci-fi books to my reading list.\n\nGameplay: Simple and accessible, but too simple. No real puzzle-solving challenge, and despite tons of dialogue options, none of it changes the story. A missed opportunity given how good the writing is.\n\nGraphics: Diorama-style rooms are genuinely beautiful — clean, warm, cozy. One note: there's a painting of Sabrina that isn't modest by Islamic standards. Would love a mod to fix that if anyone's able — otherwise the art direction is great.\n\nSound: Played with music off (personal preference around music in Islam) and the ambient sound design carried it fine — footsteps, whispers, Rumu's little motor. Voice acting is the real star here.\n\nRecommended for: anyone who wants a short, emotional, narrative-first experience — think \"interactive short story\" over \"game.\" Skip it if you want puzzle depth or replay value.\n\nTarget audience: family-friendly overall, aside from the one visual note above.",
